## Install OpenHPC Base Packages

Now OpenHPC packages can be installed. The `ohpc-base` meta-package requires a
module tool to manage the user environment, and OpenHPC provides two of them:
[Lmod](https://lmod.readthedocs.io) in the `lmod-ohpc` package and
[Environment Modules](https://modules.readthedocs.io) in the
`environment-modules-ohpc` package. Both read the OpenHPC module hierarchy and
provide the `module` command. Name the one you want alongside `ohpc-base`,
otherwise the package manager picks one of them for you. This guide uses
`{{ modules_package }}`. To add the base package and the module tool on the head
node issue the following:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Install OpenHPC base packages and the module tool -->
```bash
{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-base {{ modules_package }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

::: {.tip}
The two module tools can be installed side by side. The startup scripts
`/etc/profile.d/modules.sh` and `modules.csh`, which define the `module`
command, and `/usr/bin/modulecmd` are links managed with `alternatives`.
`environment-modules-ohpc` takes precedence over `lmod-ohpc` when both are
present. Run `alternatives --config modules.sh` to select the active tool.
Install the same module tool on the compute nodes as on the head node.
:::
